My point was that you need quite developed characters to have
the spell at a useful range. And at that point it's often of
very limited usefulness.

Note: the value of 43% failure was just as an example WRT the
value of 33% that the other poster had in mind; in that case
a valkyrie needs to have quite maxed stats and supporting gear.

In your example you need as well be quite developed and need
special gear to have the spell available at all; with a quest
prepared character (XL:14) and Wisdom of 12, and even if you
don't wear hindering armor rather have somehow acquired a robe,
you're still at 100% failure!

Play a bit with the spell calculator to observe the effects
(http://nh.gridbug.de/spells.html).

And once you're at a rate where you can cast spells at, for
example, 75% as you say, you're usually lacking the PW points
to succeed and have to wait until your PW is restored for the
next try.

The identify spell is, for valkyries, not completely useless,
but very close.

